# FormSy development kit

This package is the public Skill entry point. Read the modules below as needed
within this Skill.

## Select the current work

- When starting engineering work, switching to a separate objective, or resuming a paused one, follow the [native capture and task contract](references/progress-recording.md) to verify the actual host session and execution worktree. The existing workflow enter/select entry creates or resumes the native Task; use the native lifecycle directly only outside that workflow. Ordinary questions remain outside task capture.
- For new or resumed development, read the [development workflow](modules/formsy-sop-workflow/GUIDE.md) and the modules needed for the current stage. Use the user's existing authorization.
- For product, technical, self-check, knowledge, or aggregate documents, read the corresponding module below. Standalone documentation work stays outside a development run.
- For capture milestones and handoffs, verify the actual source and business task under the progress contract below. Resolve native capture identity independently of the workflow run.
- For reports, use the prescribed renderer below with actual inputs.

Use `cli_argv` from the project's `.formsy-sop/runtime.json` when configured.
The standalone CLI entry points are `formsy flow` and `formsy sop engine`.
Use legacy entry points only for explicitly selected compatibility with older
projects. Preserve the user's existing login and approval scope.

For workflow entry or continuation, use
`modules/formsy-sop-workflow/scripts/run_flow.py PROJECT ACTION [arguments]`.
It delegates to that exact runtime and starts/reuses an independent local Web
workbench after `enter/start/select/context`. Open the returned ready
`workbench_web.url` with Codex `open_in_codex`, browser target and
`placement=right`, then reuse the tab. Direct CLI callers use `flow web PROJECT`
for the same service. The page polls saved local artifacts; it does not need an
MCP App or render ACK. Report view availability separately and continue
authorized work. Preserve real user pauses, stage decisions and acceptance.

